# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2024-2026 Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
# Mustfile — Physical state contract for oikos-economics-accounting-dsl
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# What MUST be true about this repository. Hard requirements.
# Run with: must check
# Fix with: must fix (where a deterministic fix exists)
#
# Location: `.machine_readable/contractiles/must/Mustfile.a2ml` — the path
# standards' scripts/check-mustfile-structure.sh uses as its default. It sat at
# `.machine_readable/contractiles/Mustfile.a2ml` before 2026-10-10, where no
# consumer looks, alongside a second, different `Mustfile` (TOML-shaped,
# `version: 1` + `checks:`) at the repository root in a format nothing parses.
# That duplicate was deleted in the same commit as this move: one obligation
# file, at the path the tooling reads.

@abstract:
Physical-state invariants for the Oikos economics/accounting DSL workspace:
four Rust crates plus the repository-shape rules. These are hard requirements;
CI and the local pre-commit gate fail if any check fails.

Where a rule is already enforced by a script, the check DELEGATES to that script
instead of restating its contents. Six of the checks this file inherited from
rsr-template-repo listed root paths by hand, went stale when those paths moved
(`SECURITY.md`, `GOVERNANCE.adoc`, `MAINTAINERS.adoc`), and — because no
executable named `must` is wired into this repo's CI — stayed silently wrong.
Delegating means the file cannot drift from the gate: if the allowlist changes,
this says so, because it is the same assertion.
@end

## Repository shape

### root-shape
- description: The repository root matches .machine_readable/root-allow.txt
- run: ./scripts/check-root-shape.sh .
- severity: critical
- notes: Bidirectional. An unlisted root entry fails; a listed REQUIRED entry that is missing fails; exit 2 (no allowlist) is a setup error, not a pass. Enforced in CI by the "Estate Rules" workflow.

### root-shape-gate-can-fail
- description: The root-shape gate's self-test passes (the instrument can red)
- run: ./tests/shape/check_root_shape_test.sh
- severity: critical
- notes: A gate that has only ever printed PASS is indistinguishable from a gate that is not wired up. This is the check that keeps that from recurring here.

### security-policy
- description: A single security policy exists, in the estate's canonical location
- run: test -f .github/SECURITY.md && test ! -f SECURITY.md && test ! -f SECURITY.adoc
- severity: critical
- notes: Issue #109 item 1 / ruling D186 collapsed the root SECURITY.md pointer + root SECURITY.adoc body into one file. The negative assertions keep the duplicate from being re-created.

### code-of-conduct
- description: A code of conduct exists where GitHub can discover it
- run: test -f .github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
- severity: critical

### contributing
- description: A contribution guide exists where GitHub can discover it
- run: test -f .github/CONTRIBUTING.md
- severity: critical

### citation-metadata
- description: CITATION.cff exists and carries no unsubstituted template placeholders
- run: test -f CITATION.cff && ! grep -q '{{' CITATION.cff
- severity: warning

### ai-manifest
- description: 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml must exist at the root
- run: test -f 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml
- severity: critical
- notes: Required AT THE ROOT specifically — the standards gate table lists it in the unconditional baseline with no alternative path. It retires in the commit that mints this repo's *_chora.deed, not before.

### no-root-readme-duplication
- description: Prose lives in docs/, not beside the README
- run: test ! -f AFFIRMATION.adoc && test ! -f EXPLAINME.adoc && test ! -f GOVERNANCE.adoc && test ! -f MAINTAINERS.adoc && test ! -f PALIMPSEST.adoc && test ! -f ROADMAP.adoc && test ! -f ARCHITECTURE.adoc
- severity: warning
- notes: These were root files before 2026-10-10. The assertion is the negative because a re-created root copy is the exact regression this repo keeps suffering (SECURITY.md/SECURITY.adoc, MAINTAINERS/MAINTAINERS.adoc).

### governance-docs
- description: Governance, maintainers and CODEOWNERS exist
- run: test -f docs/GOVERNANCE.adoc && test -f docs/MAINTAINERS.adoc && test -f .github/CODEOWNERS
- severity: critical

### machine-readable-dir
- description: .machine_readable/ directory must exist, with the allowlist beside it
- run: test -d .machine_readable && test -f .machine_readable/root-allow.txt
- severity: critical

## Workflow integrity

### actions-lock-in-sync
- description: actions.lock covers every uses: ref, owns no orphans, and is transitively closed
- run: ./scripts/check-lock-sync.sh
- severity: critical
- requires: gawk
- notes: Needs gawk locally (an awk with 3-argument match()); the script exits 1 with an install hint rather than reporting a false pass. This is the check whose absence from CI caused #105 and #112.

### workflows-declare-permissions
- description: Every workflow declares top-level permissions
- run: ./.github/hooks/validate-permissions.sh
- severity: critical

### workflows-carry-spdx
- description: Every workflow carries an SPDX identifier in its leading comment block
- run: ./.github/hooks/validate-spdx.sh
- severity: critical
- notes: The leading comment BLOCK, not line 1 — `gh actions-lock` prepends its own banner to these files, so a line-1 test re-fails all of them on every lockfile refresh.

### no-dangling-doc-links
- description: Every relative link in the prose resolves
- run: ./scripts/check-doc-links.sh .
- severity: warning

## Rust workspace

### workspace-manifest
- description: Cargo.toml declares the workspace and the lockfile is committed
- run: grep -q '^\[workspace\]' Cargo.toml && test -f Cargo.lock && grep -A6 '^\[workspace\]' Cargo.toml | grep -c 'oikos-' | grep -qv '^0$'
- severity: critical
- notes: Deliberately toolchain-free. `cargo metadata` is the stronger assertion, but it cannot run on a runner with no cargo, and a shape gate that depends on which images have which SDKs gets disabled rather than fixed. The toolchain checks live in .github/workflows/ci.yml, which builds with --locked.

### no-root-src-directory
- description: There is no root src/ (source lives in the crates)
- run: test ! -d src
- severity: warning
- notes: The template allowlist requires a root src/; for a workspace it would be an empty directory that misrepresents the build, so root-allow.txt marks it optional with this reason. If a root package is ever added, revisit both.

### build-orchestration-location
- description: Guix/Nix development manifests live under build/, CI config under ci/
- run: test -f build/manifest.scm && test ! -f manifest.scm && test -f ci/.gitlab-ci.yml && test ! -f .gitlab-ci.yml
- severity: warning

## Directory Structure

### contractiles-complete
- description: Every contractile verb has a file
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Intentfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/must/Mustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Trustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/Adjustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/bust/Bustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/dust/Dustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical

### descriptiles-directory-present
- description: descriptiles directory exists with the six required files
- run: test -d .machine_readable/descriptiles && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/META.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/PLAYBOOK.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/AGENTIC.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/NEUROSYM.a2ml
- severity: critical

## State-file discipline

### no-placeholder-values
- description: No unsubstituted template placeholders remain in the machine-readable tree
- run: test -z "$(grep -rnE '\{\{[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]\{2,\}\}\}' .machine_readable/ .editorconfig .envrc CITATION.cff README.adoc docs/ 2>/dev/null | grep -vE '^[^:]+:[0-9]+:- (notes|description|corrective|severity|run):')"
- severity: critical
- notes: Matched as an ALL-CAPS `{{TOKEN}}`, not as any two braces, and with the
  contractiles' own prose excluded. Two reasons, both learned the slow way here:
  `.machine_readable/contractiles/Justfile` legitimately contains just's `{{ msrv }}`
  interpolation, and Adjustfile/Dustfile *describe* the placeholder convention, so a
  naive `{{...}}` scan reported this repo's documentation-about-placeholders as
  placeholders. A check that fires on its own explanation is a check people mute.
- notes: Inherited from rsr-template-repo, where it guards the mint. It applies here for the same reason: several files in this repo were copied from the template and never instantiated, and a leftover {{...}} is that event made visible.

## Git State

### no-untracked-contractiles
- description: All contractile files are tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -o --exclude-standard .machine_readable/contractiles/ 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical

### signed-commits
- description: All commits must be signed
- run: git verify-commit HEAD
- severity: warning
- requires: gpg
- notes: UNMET TODAY, and kept in the file anyway. Dropping an obligation because
  the repository does not satisfy it turns a contract into a description. The
  estate rule this encodes is `require-signed-commits` (see rsr-template-repo
  .github/rulesets/); this repo has no ruleset JSON checked in, so nothing
  enforces it at either end. Closing this needs an owner decision on branch
  protection plus signed commits going forward — it is not a documentation fix.
